model_solution:
Add the matrices entry by entry:

\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 0 \\ 1 & 2 \end{pmatrix}
+
\begin{pmatrix} -5 & -7 \\ 4 & -9 \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
3+(-5) & 0+(-7) \\
1+4 & 2+(-9)
\end{pmatrix}
\]

\[
=
\begin{pmatrix}
-2 & -7 \\
5 & -7
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix} -2 & -7 \\ 5 & -7 \end{pmatrix}\).

Subtract the vectors component-wise:

\[
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-5\end{pmatrix} - 4\begin{pmatrix}-1\\7\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}2\\-5\end{pmatrix} - \begin{pmatrix}-4\\28\end{pmatrix}
\]

\[
=
\begin{pmatrix}2+4\\-5-28\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}6\\-33\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix}6\\-33\end{pmatrix}\).

Compute each entry of the product:

\[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 0 \\ 5 & -3 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 8 & -2 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
2(8)+0(1) & 2(-2)+0(1) \\
5(8)+(-3)(1) & 5(-2)+(-3)(1)
\end{pmatrix}
\]

\[
=
\begin{pmatrix}
16 & -4 \\
40-3 & -10-3
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
16 & -4 \\
37 & -13
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix} 16 & -4 \\ 37 & -13 \end{pmatrix}\).

Since \((A^2)^{-1} = (A^{-1})^2\), compute:

\[
(A^{-1})^2=
\begin{pmatrix}
2 & 5\\
-1 & -3
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
2 & 5\\
-1 & -3
\end{pmatrix}
\]

\[
=
\begin{pmatrix}
2(2)+5(-1) & 2(5)+5(-3)\\
-1(2)+(-3)(-1) & -1(5)+(-3)(-3)
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
-1 & -5\\
1 & 4
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix}-1 & -5\\1 & 4\end{pmatrix}\).

Compute the matrix-vector product:

\[
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & -1 \\ -3 & 4 \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
2(3)+(-1)(-1) \\
-3(3)+4(-1)
\end{pmatrix}
\]

\[
=
\begin{pmatrix}
6+1 \\
-9-4
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
7 \\
-13
\end{pmatrix}
\]

The answer is \(\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ -13 \end{pmatrix}\).

