model_solution:
There are 13 hearts and 13 diamonds in a standard 52-card deck.

Probability both cards are hearts:

\[
\frac{13}{52}\cdot \frac{12}{51}
= \frac{1}{4}\cdot \frac{12}{51}
= \frac{3}{51}
= \frac{1}{17}
\]

Probability both cards are diamonds is the same:

\[
\frac{1}{17}
\]

Since “both hearts” and “both diamonds” cannot happen at the same time, add the probabilities:

\[
\frac{1}{17}+\frac{1}{17}=\frac{2}{17}
\]

The answer is \(\frac{2}{17}\).

