model_solution:
Bill’s total southward distance is

\[
\frac12+\frac12=1 \text{ mile}
\]

He also walks \(\frac34=0.75\) mile east. So his displacement from the starting point forms a right triangle with legs \(1\) mile and \(0.75\) mile.

The direct-line distance is the hypotenuse:

\[
\sqrt{1^2+0.75^2}
=\sqrt{1+0.5625}
=\sqrt{1.5625}
=1.25
\]

The answer is 1.25.

