Find a common denominator, which is \(6\):

\[
\frac{1}{3}=\frac{2}{6}
\]

So,

\[
\frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{3}
=\frac{1}{6}+\frac{2}{6}
=\frac{3}{6}
=\frac{1}{2}
\]

The answer is \(\frac{1}{2}\).

